  "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+\u2026+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(x+2y)}^{8},$ we have  $a=x,$ $b=2y,$ $n=8.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(x+2y)}^{8}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2y)^{8} & =(\\frac{8}{0}){(x)}^{8}{(2y)}^{0}+(\\frac{8}{1}){(x)}^{8-1}{(2y)}^{1}+(\\frac{8}{2}){(x)}^{8-2}{(2y)}^{2}+\u2026 \\\\  & =1(x)^{8}+8(x)^{7}(2y)^{1}+28(x)^{6}(2y)^{2}+\u2026 \\\\  & ={x}^{8}+16{x}^{7}{y}^{1}+28{x}^{6}(4{y}^{2})+\u2026 \\\\  & ={x}^{8}+16{x}^{7}y+112{x}^{6}{y}^{2}+\u2026\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
